 rounds: {'1': 334, '2': 376, '3': 258, '4': 140, '5': 123, '6': 62, '7': 30, '8': 14}\nCup seasons: ['2012', '2013', '2014', '2015', '2016', '2017', '2018', '2019', '2020', '2021']\n\nBrasileirao seasons: ['2012', '2013', '2014', '2015', '2016', '2017', '2018', '2019', '2020', '2021', '2022']\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"source venv/bin/activate && python -c \"\nimport csv\nwith open('data/kaggle/Libertadores_Matches.csv', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    r = csv.DictReader(f)\n    stages = {}\n    seasons = set()\n    for row in r:\n        stages[row['stage']] = stages.get(row['stage'],0)+1\n        seasons.add(row['season'])\n    print('Libertadores stages:', stages)\n    print('Libertadores seasons:', sorted(seasons))\nprint()\nwith open('data/kaggle/Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    r = csv.DictReader(f)\n    rounds = {}\n    seasons = set()\n    for row in r:\n        rounds[row['round']] = rounds.get(row['round'],0)+1\n        seasons.add(row['season'])\n    print('Cup rounds:', rounds)\n    print('Cup seasons:', sorted(seasons))\nprint()\nwith open('data/kaggle/Brasileirao_Matches.csv', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    r = csv.DictReader(f)\n    seasons = set()\n    for row in r:\n        seasons.add(row['season'])\n    print('Brasileirao seasons:', sorted(seasons))\n\"","time":{"start":1788249036470,"end":1788249036472}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"OK so FIFA 19 has a limited set of Brazilian clubs. Note: In FIFA 19, Brazilian clubs have generic players (fake names) due to licensing. Let me check if e.g. \"Flamengo\" players exist... The check shows no 'flamengo' club. The Brazilian clubs in FIFA 19 data: América FC (Minas Gerais), Atlético Mineiro, Atlético Paranaense, Bahia, Botafogo, Ceará Sporting Club, Chapecoense, Cruzeiro, Fluminense, Grêmio, Internacional, Paraná, Santos, Sport Club do Recife, Vitória.\n\nInteresting — Flamengo, Palmeiras, Corinthians, São Paulo, Vasco are missing (they were unlicensed in FIFA 19, appears as generic South American teams or not present). Wait — actually in FIFA 19, Brazilian teams were in the game with generic rosters. Flamengo etc. should be there... but the dataset may have filtered them. Let me check players with Brazilian nationality — 827 Brazilian players.\n\nAnyway, the data is what it is. The task is to build the MCP server that can query these datasets. Player queries by club will just return what's in the data. For clubs like Flamengo not in FIFA data, the query should gracefully say no players found.\n\nLet me also check the special encoding in some files. Let me check for weird characters in the BR-Football-Dataset (like the '4 de Julho EC'). Also check Libertadores stage values and team names with country suffixes like \"Nacional (URU)\".\n\nLet me look at more details:\n1. Libertadores stages\n2. Brazilian Cup rounds\n3. Date ranges in each dataset\n4. The \"Vencedor\" column values","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05bf2d666001ZOBh1cOW2pLE7l","sessionID":"ses_fa40f0460ffeYpKGnJPSwDwXVy","messageID":"msg_05bf28396001vGGY9d4IOfEr7j"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788249039922,"sessionID":"ses_fa40f0460ffeYpKGnJPSwDwXVy","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_5f5b345b2bc643ce841c7f63","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"source venv/bin/activate && python -c \"\nimport csv\n# check date ranges\nwith open('data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    r = csv.DictReader(f)\n    dates = [row['date'] for row in r]\n    print('BR-Football dates:', min(dates), '->', max(dates))\n# check for empty/odd values\nimport collections\nc = collections.Counter()\nwith open('data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    r = csv.DictReader(f)\n    for row in r:\n        if not row['home_goal'] or not row['away_goal']:\n            c['missing_goals'] += 1\n        if not row['date']:\n            c['missing_date'] += 1\nprint('missing:', c)\n\""},"output":"BR-Football dates: 2014-05-21 -> 2023-12-07\nmissing: Counter()\n","metadata":{"output":"BR-Football dates: 2014-05-21 -> 2023-12-07\nmissing: Counter()\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"source venv/bin/activate && python -c \"\nimport csv\n# check date ranges\nwith open('data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    r = csv.DictReader(f)\n    dates = [row['date'] for row in r]\n    print('BR-Football dates:', min(dates), '->', max(dates))\n# check for empty/odd values\nimport collections\nc = collections.Counter()\nwith open('data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    r = csv.DictReader(f)\n    for row in r:\n        if not row['home_goal'] or not row['away_goal']:\n            c['missing_goals'] += 1\n        if not row['date']:\n            c['missing_date'] += 1\nprint('missing:', c)\n\"","time":{"start":1788249039918,"end":1788249039921}},"id":"prt_05bf2e3d3001AgCsGRR1N27AIv","sessionID":"ses_fa40f0460ffeYpKGnJPSwDwXVy","messageID":"msg_05bf28396001vGGY9d4IOfEr7j"}}
