thletico\nodd goals rows: 2\ncup odd goals: 16\n2012 maxround 6 n 112\n2013 maxround 8 n 158\n2014 maxround 8 n 159\n2015 maxround 8 n 158\n2016 maxround 7 n 162\n2017 maxround 8 n 120\n2018 maxround 8 n 120\n2019 maxround 8 n 120\n2020 maxround 8 n 120\n2021 maxround 4 n 108\n","metadata":{"output":"finals:\n2013 2013-07-17 21:50:00 Olimpia-PAR 2 0 Atlético-MG\n2013 2013-07-24 21:50:00 Atlético-MG 2 0 Olimpia-PAR\n2014 2014-08-06 21:15:00 Nacional (PAR) 1 1 San Lorenzo\n2014 2014-08-13 21:15:00 San Lorenzo 1 0 Nacional (PAR)\n2015 2015-07-29 22:00:00 Tigres 0 0 River Plate\n2015 2015-08-05 22:00:00 River Plate 3 0 Tigres\n2016 2016-07-20 21:45:00 Independiente del Valle 1 1 Atlético Nacional\n2016 2016-07-27 21:45:00 Atlético Nacional 1 0 Independiente del Valle\n2017 2017-11-22 21:45:00 Grêmio 1 0 Lanús\n2017 2017-11-29 21:45:00 Lanús 1 2 Grêmio\n2018 2018-11-11 17:00:00 Boca Juniors 2 2 River Plate\n2018 2018-12-09 17:30:00 River Plate 3 1 Boca Juniors\n2019 2019-11-23 17:00:00 Flamengo 2 1 River Plate\n2020 2020-01-30 17:00:00 Palmeiras 1 0 Santos\nNA NA Flamengo - - Athletico\nodd goals rows: 2\ncup odd goals: 16\n2012 maxround 6 n 112\n2013 maxround 8 n 158\n2014 maxround 8 n 159\n2015 maxround 8 n 158\n2016 maxround 7 n 162\n2017 maxround 8 n 120\n2018 maxround 8 n 120\n2019 maxround 8 n 120\n2020 maxround 8 n 120\n2021 maxround 4 n 108\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"source venv/bin/activate && python << 'EOF'\nimport csv, collections\n# Libertadores finals by season; odd values\nwith open('data/kaggle/Libertadores_Matches.csv', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    rows = list(csv.DictReader(f))\nfin = [r for r in rows if r['stage']=='final']\nprint('finals:')\nfor r in fin: print(r['season'], r['datetime'], r['home_team'], r['home_goal'], r['away_goal'], r['away_team'])\nodd = [r for r in rows if not r['home_goal'].isdigit() or not r['away_goal'].isdigit()]\nprint('odd goals rows:', len(odd))\n# Cup odd values\nwith open('data/kaggle/Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    crows = list(csv.DictReader(f))\ncodd = [r for r in crows if not str(r['home_goal']).lstrip('-').isdigit()]\nprint('cup odd goals:', len(codd))\n# max round per cup season = final?\nbys = collections.defaultdict(list)\nfor r in crows: bys[r['season']].append(int(r['round']))\nfor s in sorted(bys): print(s, 'maxround', max(bys[s]), 'n', len(bys[s]))\nEOF","time":{"start":1788249840699,"end":1788249840702}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Good. Now I have full clarity. Notable:\n- Libertadores: Brazilian teams bare (\"Flamengo\", \"Athletico\", \"Vasco\"), foreign teams sometimes with country tags (\"Barcelona-EQU\", \"Nacional (URU)\", \"Guaraní-PAR\"). Also 'Rentistas ' with trailing space, and 'Real Atlético' hmm that's a Venezuelan club (Real Atlético? Actually \"Real Garcilaso\" is Peruvian; \"Real Atlético\" might be Atlético Venezuela? whatever, foreign).\n- novo: no state suffixes except they're implicit (América-MG, América-RN, Athletico-PR, Atlético-GO, Atlético-MG have suffixes; Avaí, Bahia, Corinthians, Grêmio etc. don't). \"Grêmio Prudente\" (2010 Santos... no, Grêmio Prudente = former Barueri!). Alias: \"gremio prudente\" → \"barueri\"? They're the same club (Barueri renamed Grêmio Prudente in 2010). I'll alias it.\n- FIFA: 241 empty clubs (free agents), 60 empty positions.\n\nNow design the state-hint table for bare famous names (when no state suffix in any source): \n- flamengo→RJ, fluminense→RJ, botafogo→RJ, vasco/vasco da gama→RJ, palmeiras→SP, corinthians→SP, sao paulo→SP, santos→SP, portuguesa→SP, ponte preta→SP, gremio→RS, internacional→RS, juventude→RS, caxias→RS, cruzeiro→MG, atletico→? (ambiguous! atletico mg/go/pr/ba/ac/cearense...) — bare \"Atlético\"/\"Atletico\" appears where? Libertadores has \"Atlético-MG\" and \"Atlético-PR\" (suffixed), Cup has none bare (\"Atlético - MG\" all suffixed?). Hmm \"Athletico\" bare in Libertadores = Athletico-PR (they renamed in 2019 and the Libertadores file uses the new name bare). So alias: \"athletico\"→atletico-pr. \n- sport→PE, nautico→PE, santa cruz→PE, bahia→BA, vitoria→BA, ceara→CE, fortaleza→CE, coritiba→PR, athletico paranaense→PR, parana→PR, chapecoense→SC, avai→SC, criciuma→SC, figueirense→SC, goias→GO, atletico goianiense→GO, cuiaba→MT, america mg→MG, america rn→RN / america fc natal→RN, atletico mineiro→MG.\n\nBut wait — for bare ambiguous bases like \"atletico\", \"america\", \"botafogo\", \"guarani\", \"internacional\", \"santos\", \"juventude\", \"santa cruz\", \"vitoria\", \"ypiranga\", \"operario\", \"rio branco\" — resolution needs care. My approach:\n\nTeam registry built from all match files + FIFA clubs:\n- For each (base, state) seen, register canonical id `f\"{base} {state}\"` (state lower).\n- Registry entries track: raw variants, match counts, competitions, seasons, FIFA club link.\n- Resolution of a query name:\n  1. Normalize query → (base, state).\n  2. If state given: exact `base state` in registry (after alias folding) → done. e.g. \"Botafogo RJ\" → botafogo rj. \"Atletico-PR\" → atletico pr.\n  3. If no state: \n     a. If exactly one canonical team has this base → done.\n     b. If multiple: if a STATE_HINT exists for the base (famous club) → use it (but include alternatives in output). e.g. \"Flamengo\" → flamengo rj (alt: flamengo pi). \"Atletico\" → ambiguous among atletico mg/pr/go/ba/ac/cearense — no hint (can't know) → return disambiguation message listing candidates. Hmm — but the spec example \"Palmeiras vs Santos\" etc. — famous ones get hints. For truly ambiguous ones, ask for state.\n     c. If zero: fuzzy — try alias table (e.g. \"timão\"→corinthians? skip), then prefix/substring match against bases; return candidates.\n\nAlias folding function `fold_base(base, state)` — a dict keyed by (base, state_or_None) → canonical base. And a separate `STATE_HINTS` for bare famous names.\n\nLet me define canonical base names for the big clubs (shortest