or \"nacional\"?). There are TWO Nacionals in Libertadores: Nacional (URU) and Nacional (PAR) — and \"Nacional-URU\" vs \"Nacional (URU)\" vs \"Nacional (PAR)\" vs \"Nacional-URU\". Also Nacional-AM in Cup (\"Nacional - AM\" = Nacional-AM Manaus? fast Clube vs Nacional-AM are different!). So foreign teams need disambiguation too. Canonical for foreign: append lowercased country tag: \"nacional uru\", \"nacional par\", \"barcelona equ\", \"guarani par\", \"libertad par\", \"olimpia par\", \"river plate uru\", \"universitario per\", \"delfin equ\", \"trujillanos ven\". So: extract trailing \"-EQU\"/\"(EQU)\" (3-4 letters, known country codes: URU, PAR, EQU, PER, VEN, ARG?, CHI?, COL?, BOL?, MEX?) → treat as \"country suffix\" appended to base. Let me implement: after state extraction (2-letter), check for country-tag patterns `-([A-Z]{3})$` or `\\(([A-Z]{3})\\)$` → base + \" \" + tag.lower().\n  - \"Newells Old Boys\" — apostrophe → \"newells old boys\". Fine.\n  - \"LDU\" → \"ldu\". \"Junior de Barranquilla\" → \"junior de barranquilla\" (vs Cup \"Juventude - MA\"? distinct).\n  - \"Rentistas \" trailing space → strip.\n  - \"Ind. Santa Fe\" → \"ind santa fe\". \"Independiente Del Valle\" vs \"Independiente del Valle\" — casefold handles.\n  - \"Deportivo Táchira\" accents → \"deportivo tachira\".\n  - \"Colo-Colo\" → \"colo colo\". \"O'Higgins\" → \"ohiggins\".\n\n- \"sao paulo\" — canonical \"sao paulo sp\". Note accents: \"São Paulo\" → strip accents → \"sao paulo\". \n- FIFA club mapping (FIFA club names are display names; map via same normalize + hints): \"Botafogo\"→botafogo rj, \"Grêmio\"→gremio rs, \"Santos\"→santos sp, \"Internacional\"→internacional rs, \"Vitória\"→vitoria ba, \"Paraná\"→parana pr, \"Chapecoense\"→chapecoense sc, \"Bahia\"→bahia ba, \"Ceará Sporting Club\"→ceara ce, \"Sport Club do Recife\"→sport pe, \"América FC (Minas Gerais)\"→america mg, \"Atlético Mineiro\"→atletico mg, \"Atlético Paranaense\"→atletico pr, \"Fluminense\"→fluminense rj.\n\nSTATE_HINTS (for bare famous bases, mapping base→state):\nflamengo→rj, fluminense→rj, botafogo→rj, vasco da gama→rj, bangu→rj, nova iguacu→rj? (small; skip small ones — only include where needed), palmeiras→sp, corinthians→sp, sao paulo→sp, santos→sp, portuguesa→sp, ponte preta→sp, guarani→sp, gremio→rs, internacional→rs, juventude→rs, caxias→rs, cruzeiro→mg, atletico mineiro... (folded already), sport→pe, nautico→pe, santa cruz→pe, bahia→ba, vitoria→ba, ceara→ce, fortaleza→ce, coritiba→pr, parana→pr, chapecoense→sc, avai→sc, criciuma→sc, figueirense→sc, goias→go, cuiaba→mt, brusque→sc?, botafogo sp→? (botafogo sp is in BR-Football with explicit sp; bare \"botafogo\" → RJ hint).\n\nWait, there's a subtlety: hints should only apply when the bare base isn't uniquely resolvable. \"Corinthians\" appears bare in novo/Libertadores AND as \"Corinthians - SP\" in Cup/BR — registry will have \"corinthians sp\" from both (state extraction). Bare \"corinthians\" from novo registers... hmm — when loading novo's \"Corinthians\" (no state), do I register it as \"corinthians\" (stateless) or apply hint → \"corinthians sp\"? \n\nDecision: during registry build, EVERY raw name resolves to a canonical id. For bare names with a hint → use hint. For bare names without hint and no other club with same base+state anywhere → stateless id (e.g., \"bragantino pa\" has state... ). Bare stateless foreign names → keep stateless. So \"Corinthians\" → \"corinthians sp\". \n\nBut what about \"Botafogo\" bare? Hint RJ → \"botafogo rj\". Does bare \"Botafogo\" (Libertadores) mean Botafogo-RJ? Yes.\n\"Santos\" bare (Libertadores/FIFA/BR-Football) → hint SP → \"santos sp\". Good.\n\"Internacional\" bare → \"internacional rs\". \"Internacional SC\" (EC Internacional SC / Internacional - SC) → \"internacional sc\". \n\"Vasco\" bare → \"vasco da gama rj\". \n\"Athletico\" bare → \"atletico pr\" (alias athletico→atletico when... hmm \"athletico\" is a distinct base; fold (base=\"athletico\") → \"atle