ter state extraction: \"ec internacional sc\" → state \"sc\", base \"ec internacional\". Then fold (\"ec internacional\", sc) → (\"internacional\", sc). Good.\n- \"portuguesa desportos\" → (\"portuguesa\", \"sp\")\n- \"macae esporte\" → (\"macae\", \"rj\")\n- \"esportivo bento goncalves\" → (\"esportivo\", \"rs\")\n- \"operario ferroviario esporte c\" → (\"operario\", \"pr\")\n- \"operario fc\" → (\"operario\", \"ms\")? BR-Football 'Operario FC MS' → state ms, base \"operario fc\" → fold → (\"operario\",\"ms\"). \n- \"boavista sport club\" → (\"boavista\", \"rj\")\n- \"aquidauanense futebol clube\" → (\"aquidauanense\", \"ms\")\n- \"parnahyba sc\" → (\"parnahyba\", \"pi\") — wait \"Parnahyba S.c - PI\": state strip gives base \"parnahyba s c\"?? Hmm: \"parnahyba s.c - PI\" → after state extraction: \"parnahyba s.c\" → dots removed → \"parnahyba sc\" → hmm that's \"sc\" as in \"S.C.\" (Sport Club) not state. Fold (\"parnahyba sc\", pi) → (\"parnahyba\",\"pi\"). OK but note: state extraction happens on the string with \"- PI\" suffix — yes extracted \"pi\" first. Good. But CAREFUL: what about names genuinely ending in \"- SC\" (Santa Catarina suffix)? e.g. \"Avai-SC\" → state sc. Both interpretations exist but per-team it's consistent. For \"parnahyba s.c\" the state was already PI, so trailing \"sc\" is part of name — handled by fold. \n- \"rio branco vn\" → (\"rio branco\", \"es\")\n- \"independente de tucurui\" → (\"independente\", \"pa\")\n- \"santa quiteria futebol clube\" → (\"santa quiteria\", \"ma\")\n- \"sao domingos futebol clube\" → (\"sao domingos\", \"se\")\n- \"arapongas esporte clube\" → (\"arapongas\", \"pr\")\n- \"paulista futebol clube\" → (\"paulista\", \"sp\")\n- \"desportiva ferroviaria\" → (\"desportiva\", \"es\")\n- \"real noroeste capixaba\" → (\"real noroeste\", \"es\")\n- \"flamengo do piaui\" → (\"flamengo\", \"pi\")\n- \"fluminense de feira\" → (\"fluminense\", \"ba\")? Fluminense de Feira Hx — yes BA club. \n- \"guarani de juazeiro\" → (\"guarani\", \"ce\")? Hmm — wait, actually Guarani de Juazeiro vs \"Guarani - CE\" in Cup: Cup lists BOTH \"Guarani - CE\" AND \"Guarani de Juazeiro - CE\" — if same club, why both spellings? Different rounds/years maybe. Risky either way; merging is more useful than not. I'll fold (\"guarani de juazeiro\", ce) → (\"guarani\", \"ce\"). Hmm, but actually I'm not 100% sure they're the same club... Guarani EC de Juazeiro do Norte — and \"Guarani - CE\"... The famous CE Guarani IS from Juazeiro do Norte. OK fold.\n- \"abc\" — \"A.b.c.\" → dots removed → \"abc\" + RN → \"abc rn\". \"ABC - RN\" → \"abc rn\". consistent, no fold needed.\n- \"crb\"/\"c r b\": \"C.r.b. - AL\" → dots → \"crb\"+\"al\". \"C. R. B. - AL\" → \"c r b\"+al?? \"C. R. B.\" — dots removed without space: \"C. R. B.\" → \"C R B\" → tokens \"c\",\"r\",\"b\" — NOT \"crb\"! Because spaces between letters remain. Damn. So \"c r b\" vs \"crb\" mismatch. Fix: after state extraction and dots-removal, ALSO collapse single-letter token runs: join consecutive single-char tokens: \"c r b\" → \"crb\". \"a b c\" → \"abc\". Does that break anything? \"a b c\" only appears in such abbreviations. Safe: collapse runs of single-character tokens into one token. \"Xv de Piracicaba\": \"xv\" is 2 chars — safe. \n- \"sampaio correa\" — consistent after accents.\n- \"sao luiz\"/\"são luiz\" rs — consistent.\n- \"vila nova\"/\"villa nova\" — distinct (GO vs MG) — states differ, keep both bases as-is: \"vila nova go\", \"villa nova mg\". No conflict.\n- \"cuiaba\" vs \"cuiaba mt\"? novo doesn't have; Brasileirao \"Cuiaba-MT\" → \"cuiaba mt\"; BR-Football? probably \"Cuiaba\". Hint cuiaba→mt. \n- \"Red Bull Bragantino\" (Brasileirao/Libertadores/Cup/BR) → \"red bull bragantino sp\"; novo 90s? no (novo ends 2019, RB Bragantino promoted 2019 — novo has no Bragantino; Cup has \"Bragantino - SP\" (old CA Bragantino 90s!) AND \"Red Bull Bragantino - SP\". Same club lineage (Red Bull bought Bragantino in 2019). Merge? \"Bragantino - SP\" 1990s = Clube Atlético Bragantino; \"Red Bull Bragantino\" = same club renamed. I'll fold (\"bragantino\", sp) → (\"red bull bragantino\", sp)?? Hmm — or the reverse: canonical \"red bull bragantino\" since modern. But CA Bragantino purists... it's the same legal entity (Red Bull Bragantino). Fold \"bragantino\" → \"red bull bragantino\". OK. Also \"Bragantino - PA\" is a DIFFERENT club (Bragantino-PA? there's a \"Bragantino Clube do Pará\"?) — only fold with state SP.\n- \"Athletico Paranaense - PR\" (Cup) & \"Atlético Paranaense - PR\" → folds → atletico pr. And Brasileirao \"Atletico-PR\" → atletico pr. novo \"Athletico-PR\" (2019) → atletico pr. BR-Football \"Athletico Paranaense\" (no state) → ALIAS forces pr. Consistent!\n- novo \"Grêmio Prudente\" → fold → barueri sp; novo \"Barueri\" → barueri sp (hint sp — add \"barueri\"→sp hint).\n\nForeign teams (Libertadores): no hints; they stay as loaded (with country tags appended where present). Bare foreign: \"Boca Juniors\" → \"boca juniors\". Two \"Independiente del Valle\" spellings — casefold handles. \"Nacional (URU)\" → paren content... wait — I planned paren-stripping for country tags: extract \"(URU)\" as country tag → \"nacional uru\". \"Nacional-URU\" → country tag via `-URU` → \"nacional uru\". \"Nacional (PAR)\" → \"nacional par\". \"Nacional - AM\" (Cup, Brazilian) → \"nacional am\". No bare \"Nacional\" in Libertadores — good. \"Guaraní (PAR)\"/\"Guaraní-PAR\" → \"guarani par\". Note: \"Guarani\" (bare, Brazilian, SP hint) vs \"guarani par\" (Paraguayan) — distinct ids. Careful in matching: exact \"guarani\" → hint SP → \"guarani sp\". Good.\n\"LDU\" → \"ldu\". \"Junior de Barranquilla\" → \"junior de barranquilla\". \"Ind. Santa Fe\" → dots removed → \"ind santa fe\". \"O'Higgins\" → apostrophe removed → \"ohiggins\". \"Colo-Colo\" → \"colo colo\". \"Newells Old Boys\" → \"newells old boys\". \"Vélez Sarsfield\" → \"velez sarsfield\". \"Mineros de Guaiana\" → as-is. \"Always Ready\" → \"always ready\". \"Sporting Cristal\", \"Melgar\", \"Binacional\", \"Cobresal\", \"Huachipato\", \"Palestino\", \"Unión Española\"... fine.\n\"Deportivo Anzoátegui\" → \"deportivo anzoategui\". \"Estudiantes de Mérida\" → \"estudiantes de merida\" vs \"Estudiantes\" (ARG) — distinct. \"Talleres\", \"Tigre\", \"Tigres\", \"Tijuana\" — fine. \"San José\" → \"san jose\" (Bolivia). \"The Strongest\" → fine. \"Universitario (PER)\"/\"Universitario-PER\" → \"universitario per\". \"Universitario de Sucre\" → Bolivia, distinct. \"Zamora\", \"Zulia\", \"Caracas\", \"Monagas\", \"Trujillanos (VEN)\" → \"trujillanos ven\". \"Deportivo Cali\" vs \"Deportivo Táchira\" → fine. \"América de Cali\" → \"america de cali\" — hmm wait, bare \"america\" hint? No — \"america de cali\" is its own base (state none, foreign). Fine. \"Argentinos Juniors\", \"Arsenal Sarandí\", \"Atlético Nacional\" (COL), \"Atlético Tucumán\" — hmm \"atletico nacional\" — foreign, no state — base \"atletico nacional\". Distinct from Brazilian atleticos. OK. \"Barcelona-EQU\"/\"Delfín-EQU\" → \"barcelona equ\", \"delfin equ\". \"Emelec\". \"Deportes Iquique\", \"Deportes Tolima\" vs \"Tolima\" — two spellings of the same Colombian club! \"Deportes Tolima\" and \"Tolima\" both in Libertadores. Merge? alias (\"tolima\", None) → (\"deportes tolima\", None). Yes, add.\n\"Rentistas \" → strip → \"rentistas\". \"River Plate\" (ARG) vs \"River Plate-URU\" → \"river plate\" vs \"river plate uru\". \"Real Garcilaso\" → \"real garcilaso\" (Peru). \"Real Atlético\"?? — hmm, odd one. Venezuelan? \"Real Atlético\" might be a data quirk for \"Atlético\" (VEN)? I'll leave as-is.\n\nOK, the country-tag extraction: pattern `-([A-Za-z]{3})$` where the 3-letter code is uppercase in original OR in known set {URU, PAR, EQU, PER, VEN, ARG, CHI, COL, BOL, MEX, ECU}. And `\\(([A-Za-z]{3})\\)$`. I'll restrict to a known set to avoid false positives.\n\nAlso — Brazilian Cup names like \"A.b.c. - RN\": state suffix \" - RN\" extracted first (2-let