eam, initialization_options)` — and initialization options come from `server.initialize_options()`. Let me fix: `server.run(*server_streams, server.initialize_options())`. But there's an ordering problem — the client must send initialize first... Actually the standard pattern from mcp tests in 2.x:\n\n```python\nasync with create_client_server_memory_streams() as (client_streams, server_streams):\n    async with ClientSession(*client_streams) as session:\n        server_task = asyncio.create_task(server.run(*server_streams, server.initialize_options()))\n        await session.initialize()\n        ...\n```\n\nThe server.run processes the initialize request from the client. Let me check the signature of MCPServer.run.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05c025488001J8vElxa5MD8FW4","sessionID":"ses_fa40f0460ffeYpKGnJPSwDwXVy","messageID":"msg_05c021bdc0017gbpOXSJIczopj"}}
