(RJ)\" or raw prettiest variant\n```\n\nTeam registry:\n```python\n@dataclass\nclass TeamEntity:\n    team_id: str\n    display_name: str\n    state: str | None\n    variants: set[str]       # raw names seen\n    sources: set[str]\n    match_count: int\n    fifa_club_names: set[str]\n    competitions: dict[str, set[str]]  # comp -> seasons\n```\n\nResolution result: `Resolution(team_id, display, ambiguous: bool, alternatives: list[TeamEntity], error: str|None)`.\n\nNow, careful design of normalize functions:\n\n```python\ndef strip_accents(s): ...\ndef collapse_ws(s): ...\n\n_STATE_NAMES = {'minas gerais': 'mg', 'sao paulo': 'sp', ...}  # for parenthetical \"(Minas Gerais)\"\n\nCOUNTRY_TAGS = {'URU','PAR','EQU','PER','VEN','ARG','CHI','COL','BOL','MEX','ECU'}\n\ndef parse_team_name(raw) -> (base, state, country):\n    s = raw.strip()\n    # extract parenthetical state name or country tag\n    m = re.search(r'\\(([^)]+)\\)\\s*$', s)\n    paren = None\n    if m:\n        paren = m.group(1).strip()\n        s = s[:m.start()].strip()\n        if strip_accents(paren).lower() in _STATE_NAMES:\n            state_from_paren = _STATE_NAMES[...]\n        elif paren.upper() in COUNTRY_TAGS:\n            country = paren.lower()\n        else:\n            # antigo Esporte Clube Barreira etc -> drop\n    # country tag suffix \"-EQU\"\n    m = re.search(r'[-–]\\s*([A-Za-z]{3})$', s)\n    if m and m.group(1).upper() in COUNTRY_TAGS:\n        country = m.group(1).lower(); s = s[:m.start()].strip()\n    # state suffix\n    m = re.search(r'(?:^|\\s|[-–])\\s*([A-Za-z]{2})$', s)\n    if m and not country:  # states only for Brazilian teams\n        cand = m.group(1).lower()\n        if cand in VALID_UFS: state = cand; s = s[:m.start()].strip()\n    # now normalize base\n    b = strip_accents(s).lower()\n    b = b.replace('.', '')        # a.b.c -> abc, s.francisco -> sfrancisco\n    b = re.sub(r\"[^\\w\\s]\", ' ', b)  # hyphens/apostrophes -> space\n    b = collapse_ws(b)\n    b = join_single_letters(b)    # \"c r b\" -> \"crb\"\n    return b, state, country\n```\n\nWait — careful with `_STATE_NAMES`: \"(Minas Gerais)\" → \"mg\". But also bare state suffix \"-MG\". Also for Brazilian VALID_UFS set: all 27 UF codes.\n\nHmm, one problem: the state-suffix regex on \"Avai-SC\" → base \"avai\", state \"sc\". On \"Corinthians-SP\" → \"corinthians\"/\"sp\". On \"Atletico-GO\" → \"atletico\"/\"go\". Good. But on foreign \"Barcelona-EQU\" — handled before by country tag. What about a hypothetical Brazilian name where final 2 letters aren't a state? e.g., \"B.?\" — I can't think of one; VALID_UFS check + requiring separator handles most.\n\nEdge: \"Sampaio Correa - MA\" → sep \"-\" + \"ma\" → state ma ✓. \"Juventude - MA\" ✓. \"A.b.c. - RN\" → state rn; base \"a.b.c.\" → \"abc\" ✓. \"C.r.a.c. - GO\" → \"crac\" ✓. \"Pstc - PR\" → \"pstc\" ✓. \"Fc Cascavel - PR\" → base \"fc cascavel\", state pr ✓. \"Serra F. C. - ES\" → base \"serra f c\"?? dots removed: \"serra f. c.\" → \"serra f c\" → join_single_letters: \"f\" and \"c\" are consecutive single-letter tokens → \"fc\" → \"serra fc\" ✓. \"Vitoria F. C. - ES\" → \"vitoria fc\" ✓. \"Boavista Sport Club (antigo Esporte Clube Barreira) - RJ\" → paren \"antigo Esporte Clube Barreira\" — not a state name, not a country tag → dropped ✓ → \"boavista sport club\" + rj → ALIASES fold → boavista/rj ✓. \"América FC (Minas Gerais)\" → paren state name → mg; base \"america fc\" → fold (\"america fc\", mg) → (\"america\", mg) ✓. \"Nacional (URU)\" → country uru; base \"nacional\" → id \"nacional uru\" ✓. \"Guaraní (PAR)\" → \"guarani par\" ✓. \"Barcelona-EQU\" → \"barcelona equ\" ✓. \"Nacional-URU\" → \"nacional uru\" ✓. \"River Plate-URU\" → \"river plate uru\" ✓. \"Universitario (PER)\" → \"universitario per\" ✓. \"O'Higgins\" → apostrophe → space → \"ohiggins\"?? \"O'Higgins\" → `re.sub(r\"[^\\w\\s]\", ' ', \"o'higgins\")` → \"o higgins\" → collapse → \"o higgins\" → join single letters: \"o\" single-letter followed by