ign. If MULTIPLE states exist for that base → need disambiguation: use hardcoded FAMOUS_HINTS for the famous ones (flamengo→rj etc.), else keep stateless (its own id, won't merge with stateful ones — slight data fragmentation for small clubs but safe).\n   \n   Wait — but ordering matters: \"Corinthians\" bare (novo) and \"Corinthians - SP\" (Cup) — pass 1 collects both; \"corinthians\" appears stateless once + (\"corinthians\",\"sp\") once → auto-assign stateless→sp ✓.\n   - \"Botafogo\" bare (Libertadores/BR/FIFA) + (\"botafogo\",\"rj\"),(\"botafogo\",\"pb\"),(\"botafogo\",\"sp\") → multiple → FAMOUS_HINTS['botafogo']='rj' → assign rj ✓.\n   - \"Santos\" bare + (\"santos\",\"sp\") & (\"santos\",\"ap\") → hint sp ✓.\n   - \"Internacional\" bare + rs & sc → hint rs ✓.\n   - \"Juventude\" bare + rs & ma → hint rs ✓.\n   - \"Vitoria\" bare + ba & es → hint ba ✓.\n   - \"Gremio\" bare + rs only?? — 'Gremio RS' gives (\"gremio\",\"rs\"); any other \"gremio XX\"? 'Gremio Anapolis' is base 'gremio anapolis' (different base!) ✓. So unique → auto rs ✓.\n   - \"Atletico Mineiro\" → folded to ('atletico','mg') by alias → then base 'atletico' has states mg, pr, go, ba, ac, + ('atletico cearense','ce') different base ✓. Bare 'atletico'? Does any raw bare \"Atlético\"/\"Atletico\" exist? Libertadores NA row: 'Athletico' → fold → ('atletico','pr') explicitly ✓. Cup: all \"Atlético - XX\" suffixed ✓. So no bare 'atletico' — good, no ambiguity at registration. Only user QUERIES for \"Atletico\" hit ambiguity → runtime disambiguation ✓.\n   - \"America\" bare? No raw bare América (checked: Cup all suffixed; BR has 'America MG'/'America RN' suffixed-in-base; novo 'América-MG'/'América-RN' suffixed). FIFA folded. ✓ no registration ambiguity.\n   - \"Ceara\" bare + (\"ceara\",\"ce\") unique → auto ce ✓.\n   - \"Bahia\" bare + (\"bahia\",\"ba\") unique ✓ (any \"bahia XX\"? 'Bahia de Feira - BA' base 'bahia de feira' different ✓).\n   - \"Sport\" bare + (\"sport\",\"pe\") unique ✓.\n   -