unique ✓. \"Gremio\" ✓. \"Internacional\" hint ✓. \"Botafogo\" hint ✓. \"Santos\" hint ✓. \"Vitoria\" hint ✓. \"Ceara\" ✓. \"Fortaleza\" + ce unique ✓. \"Sport\" ✓. \"Bahia\" ✓.\n\nThis auto-derivation handles 90% of cases with a tiny hint table. \n\nFor the remaining explicit folds (base renames), I'll have the ALIASES table as planned. Let me also add folds for BR-Football \"FC\"/\"EC\"/\"SC\"/\"CA\"/\"GE\"/\"CE\"/\"URT\"-prefixed variants and \"X EC\"/\"X FC\" suffixes... CAREFUL: I can NOT strip generic \"EC/FC/SC\" tokens — \"SC Genus\" vs \"Genus\", \"EC Vitoria\" vs \"Vitoria ES\" collision... Strip-generic would merge \"EC Internacional SC\"→\"internacional sc\" (good) but also \"SC Genus\"→\"genus\" (good — Cup 'Genus - RO' exists!) and \"CE Aimore\"→\"aimore\" (good) and \"CA Parana\"→\"parana\" (DANGER: merges with Paraná-PR the famous club! Is \"CA Parana\" = CA Paranaense? hmm). And \"URT MG\"→\"urt\"... and \"Boavista SC Saquarema\"→\"boavista saquarema\" hmm.\n\nGeneric prefix-stripping is too risky (CA Parana case). I'll stick with the explicit alias table + auto-state-derivation. For entries like 'Boavista SC Saquarema', 'SC Genus', 'CE Aimore', 'CE Dom Bosco', 'CEO Varzeagrandense', 'AE Altos', 'Amadense EC', 'Cordino EC', 'Tocantinopolis EC', 'Toledo EC', 'Sinop FC', 'Sousa EC', 'URT MG'/'URT', 'Nova Mutum EC'/'Nova Mutum', 'Tombense MG'/'Tombense', 'Tupi MG'/'Tupi', 'Vilhenense EC', 'Nova Venecia FC', 'Real Ariquemes', 'Porto Velho EC', 'Azuriz FC', 'Macae Esporte FC', 'Democrata GV', 'Metropolitano Maringa PR', 'Monsoon FC', 'Afogados da Ingazeira FC', 'Falcon', 'Real FC', 'Humaita', 'Camboriu', 'Marcilio Dias', 'Guaratingueta', 'Mogi Mirim', 'Pouso Alegre', 'Real Ariquemes', 'Iguatu', 'Suzano SP'...\n\nRather than exhaustively aliasing every small club (diminishing returns — these appear in only ONE source so no cross-file merge is needed for them!), I only need aliases where the same club appears in MULTIPLE sources with different spellings, or where teams play across files. Small one-source clubs just need a stable id.\n\nLet me be pragmatic: my alias table covers the cases identified above where multi-source merging matters ( Serie A/B clubs, Cup main clubs, Libertadores, FIFA). One-source small clubs keep their parsed id (with state if derivable from another source's variant).\n\nHmm — but wait: BR-Football Serie B/C clubs DO interact with Cup clubs (same clubs appear in both!). E.g. 'CRB' (BR) vs 'Crb - AL' (Cup) → BR 'CRB' bare → base 'crb' — auto-state: any ('crb', state) from other files? Cup 'C.r.b. - AL' → ('crb','al') ✓ → auto-assign ✓. \n\nAnd 'ASA' bare (BR) + Cup 'A.s.a. - AL'/'Asa - AL' → ('asa','al') ✓ auto.\n\n'ABC' (BR) + Cup 'ABC - RN'/'Abc - RN' → ('abc','rn') ✓ auto.\n\n'Sampaio Correa' (BR) + Cup 'Sampaio Corrêa - MA' ✓ auto.\n\n'Confianca' + Cup 'Confiança - SE' ✓. 'AD Confianca' (BR) → base 'ad confianca' — different base! fold ('ad confianca',None)→('confianca','se')? AD Confiança = same club (Associação Desportiva Confiança). Add fold. Similarly 'AD Frei Paulistano' → ('frei paulistano','se') fold (Cup 'Frei Paulistano - SE' ✓).\n\nOK. The auto-state mechanism handles most; explicit table for renames. Let me also double-check 'Ypiranga' bare context and 'CA Parana' context quickly.\n\nAlso 'Moto Club de São Luís' vs Cup 'Moto Club - MA' → fold ('moto club de sao luis',None)→('moto club','ma') ✓ add. 'Moto Clube' (BR) — base 'moto clube' — fold ('moto clube',None)→('moto club','ma') ✓.\n\nAnd 'Fast Clube' ✓ same both. 'Trem AP' ✓. 'Penarol AM' ✓. \n\nOK — enough analysis. One quick check on 'Ypiranga' bare and 'CA Parana' and 'Real FC' contexts, then write all the code.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05c0c248f001VnQUGvE1sSgXMa","sessionID":"ses_fa40f0460ffeYpKGnJPSwDwXVy","messageID":"msg_05c07f7520016wztfwtkLSir7G"}}
