 A had 380 matches. Some 2014 season matches were played in Jan-Mar 2015?? No — hmm, Jan-Mar 2015 has 19 matches. Those would be 2014-season spillover → reassigned to 2014 → 281+19=300? Still not 380. So br_football 2014 is just incomplete (~300). Hmm wait — 281 + 19 = 300 — let me recompute: Serie A 2014 shows 281 AFTER reassignment (includes Jan-Mar 2015 matches). So br_football 2014 Serie A is incomplete (~300 of 380).\n- Jan-Mar matches exist across many years (2017: 64, 2018: 71, 2019: 60, 2020: 70, 2022: 55, 2023: 54)... These can't all be spillover! Serie A 2017 season ran May-Dec 2017 — what are 64 matches in Jan-Mar 2018?? Hmm — OH WAIT. I bet these are state championships (Campeonato Paulista etc.)? No — this file only has Serie A/B/C + Copa do Brasil. Hmm, 64 matches in Jan-Mar 2018 for... which tournaments? Let me think — Copa do Brasil! The Copa do Brasil's FIRST ROUND is played in January-February! Yes! Copa do Brasil first round happens Jan-Feb (e.g. 2018 CdB first round Feb 2018). So Jan-Mar matches are legitimately Copa do Brasil first-round matches of that calendar year — NOT spillover!\n\nSo the reassignment rule is WRONG for Copa do Brasil (would move 2018 CdB first-round matches into the 2017 season!). And the 2021 spike (225 Jan-Mar 2021) includes BOTH 2020 Serie A spillover AND 2021 CdB first round (Feb 2021). Let me quantify: Jan-Mar 2021 by tournament.\n\nPer-tournament spillover rules:\n- Copa do Brasil: season = calendar year (first rounds in Jan/Feb belong to that year's edition) — NO reassignment.\n- Serie A/B/C: spillover possible (2020→2021 COVID). Which Jan-Mar matches are Serie A? 2021 only? Let me check Jan-Mar Serie A/B/C matches by year. If Serie A/B/C Jan-Mar matches only occur in 2021 (and maybe 2021 early = 2020 season), reassign ONLY Serie A/B/C with month<=3 to previous year. For other years, Serie A/B/C in Jan-Mar... let me check.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05c20295b001JytedmOIg7VoRk","sessionID":"ses_fa40f0