ment, Serie A season counts become: 2014: 281, 2015: 380 (379+1), 2016: 378, 2017-2019: 380, 2020: 375+111=486?? WAIT no. Let me recompute: Serie A 2020 (by date): 375, of which how many are in Jan-Mar 2020? From the table: Serie A Jan-Mar only 2016(1) and 2021(111). So Serie A 2020 = 375 all Apr-Dec 2020. Reassigning the 111 early-2021 matches to 2020: 2020 → 486?! That can't be right — the 2020 season had 380 matches.\n\nHmm! 375 + 111 = 486 > 380. So the early-2021 Serie A matches are NOT all 2020-season spillover — some are... wait, the 2021 Serie A season started in May 2021. Jan-Apr 2021 Serie A matches (111) must be 2020-season postponed matches. But then 2020 season total = 375 + 111 = 486?? More than 380. Contradiction!\n\nUnless... the 2020 Serie A season indeed had matches in early 2021 AND br_football ALSO has 2020-season matches dated within 2020 that include... 375 in Apr-Dec 2020. Real 2020 Serie A: 380 matches between Aug 2020 and Feb 2021. If ~111 were played Jan-Feb 2021, only ~269 should be in 2020 — but br_football shows 375 in 2020. So 375 + 111 = 486 ≈ 380 + 106 extra. Something's off — maybe br_football contains DUPLICATE rows! Let me check for duplicates in br_football Serie A (same teams + same date).\n\nActually — wait. Maybe many of those Jan-Feb 2021 \"Serie A\" matches are duplicates of matches already dated in 2020? Or... the 2021 season itself: 380 matches Apr-Dec 2021 + the file's 2021 total was 491 → 491 - 380 = 111 played Jan-Mar 2021 → those are 2020 spillover. And 2020: 375 + 111 = 486 ≠ 380. So either duplicates or the 2020 season in this file is odd. Let me check duplicates and also the actual date range of \"2020\" and early-2021 Serie A matches.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05c20b668001OJlAtqz1mNVPnl","sessionID":"ses_fa40f0460ffeYpKGnJPSwDwXVy","messageID":"msg_05c202aed0017mCoGS7cD8kZLa"}}
