first one whose\n-    playable match count is at least 80% of the best available source is\n+    playable match count is at least 85% of the best available source is\n     chosen.  This keeps the dedicated files in charge (round labels,\n     cleaner names) while ensuring materially incomplete seasons fall back\n     to a fuller source -- e.g. Série A 2022 (299 playable rows in\n     Brasileirao_Matches.csv due to 'NA' scores) falls back to\n-    BR-Football's 379, and Copa do Brasil 2021 (unplayed round with 'NA'\n-    scores in the dedicated cup file) falls back to BR-Football's\n-    complete bracket.\n+    BR-Football's 379, and Copa do Brasil 2021 (unplayed round-of-16 with\n+    'NA' scores, and no final, in the dedicated cup file) falls back to\n+    BR-Football's complete bracket.\n     \"\"\"\n     key = (competition, season)\n     if key in self.default_source:\n         return self.default_source[key]\n@@ -553,9 +553,9 @@\n     best = max(counts.values(), default=0)\n     chosen = None\n     if best:\n         for source in SOURCE_PRIORITY.get(competition, []):\n-            if counts.get(source, 0) >= 0.8 * best:\n+            if counts.get(source, 0) >= _SOURCE_COMPLETENESS_RATIO * best:\n                 chosen = source\n                 break\n     self.default_source[key] = chosen\n     return chosen\n","additions":5,"deletions":5},"truncated":false},"title":"soccer_mcp/data_loader.py","time":{"start":1788252350128,"end":1788252350130}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Excellent! The source selection now works perfectly:\n- serie_a: 2003-2011 → novo, 2012-2021 → brasileirao, 2022-2023 → br_football ✓\n- copa_do_brasil: 2012-2021 → cup file... WAIT — 2021 still picks brazilian_cup_matches! Expected br_football (cup 92 playable vs br_football 132). 92/132 = 0.697 < 0.8 → should switch. Let me check the actual counts in the dataset: cup 2021 playable = 108-16 = 92. br_football copa 2021 = 132. Hmm — but wait, `source_priority_for` computes counts from `self._by_comp_season[('copa_do_brasil', '2021')]` — br_football copa 2021 = 132? Earlier raw count was 111 matches with date year 2021. Hmm, earlier I computed 111 by date[:4]=='2021'. But some early-2022 Copa matches... no wait — Copa do Brasil has no reassignment, so br_football copa 2021 = 111? Earlier output \"Copa do Brasil {2021: 132}\" — that was with month≤3 reassigned (2021 gained early-2022 matches: 55 Jan-Mar 2022 minus...). Hmm: 111 (raw 2021) + early-2022 copa matches (2022-01/02/03 = part of 55) = 132?? That would mean 21 early-2022 matches moved INTO 2021 — but that's WRONG for Copa do Brasil (early-2022 matches = 2022 edition first round!).\n\n  WAIT — no. Look at my implementation: for copa_do_brasil, season = year (no reassignment). So br_football copa 2021 = raw count of date-year 2021 = 111. But the printed table earlier (with the reassignment applied to ALL tournaments) said 132 — that was just my exploratory script, not the implementation. In the implementation, copa keeps calendar year: 2021 = 111, 2022 = 116 (raw 117 minus early-2022 matches that belong to... no wait — no reassignment → 2022 = raw 2022 count = 117).\n\n  So for copa 2021: cup file 92 vs br_football 111 → 92/111 = 0.83 ≥ 0.8 → CUP FILE WINS. Hmm! But the cup file's 2021 data is BROKEN (round 4 all NA = round-of-16 unplayed) — it's MISSING the quarterfinals, semis, and final!\n\n  The 80% rule fails here because br_football's 111 isn't dramatically more than cup's 92. The REAL issue: cup 2021 lacks its final. The completeness-by-count heuristic can't detect \"missing final\" when 83% of matches are present.\n\n  Options:\n  a) Special-case: hard-code source override for copa_do_brasil 2021 → br_football. With a comment explaining. Pragmatic, deterministic, honest.\n  b) Finals-aware completeness: check whether the season's default-source data contains a \"final\" (detectable). Too circular.\n  c) Lower threshold to 70%: copa 2021 → br_football (92/111=0.83 ≥ 0.7 → still cup!). No — lower threshold makes the cup file MORE likely to stay. I need the opposite: threshold ~85% → 0.83 < 0.85 → switch to br_football. Check side effects of 85%: serie_a 2020: brasileirao 380 (best) ✓ stays. serie_a 2022: 299/379=0.789 <0.85 → br_football ✓. copa 2016: cup 162 vs br_football 203: 0.798 < 0.85 → br_football ✓ (fine). copa 2019: cup 120 vs br_football 127: 0.945 ≥ 0.85 → cup ✓. copa 2015: cup 158 vs 128: cup is best ✓. copa 2020: cup 120 vs br_football 81: cup best ✓. serie_a 2014: brasileirao 380 vs br_football ~300 (281+19... wait with reassignment: br_football serie_a 2014 = 281+19 = 300): 380 best → brasileirao ✓. serie_a 2015: brasileirao 380 vs br_football 380 vs novo 380 → brasileirao ✓. serie_a 2016: brasileirao 379 vs novo 380 vs br_football 378: 379/380 = 0.997 ≥ 0.85 → brasileirao ✓ (better than novo's phantom draw!). serie_a 2021: brasileirao 380 vs br_football 380 → brasileirao ✓.\n\n  85% threshold works for every case. Let me set 0.85. Also verify copa 2021 picks br_football after the change: 92/111 = 0.829 < 0.85 ✓.\n\nAlso note: Fla-Flu 44 matches with dedup — sanity: Flamengo vs Fluminense from 2012-2023 in Serie A (22 seasons × 2 = ~42?) — 2003-2011 novo also has Fla-Flu! Why only 44? serie_a:42, copa:2. Hmm — 2003-2023 Serie A would be ~40-44 meetings... 2003-2023 = 21 seasons × 2 = 42 ✓ exactly. Copa 2 (2023 semifinal? Flamengo vs Fluminense 2023 CdB semifinal ✓). But wait — should there be more from 2003-2011 (novo)? 9 seasons × 2 = 18 of those 42 ✓ consistent. OK.\n\nStandings 2019: Flamengo 90 pts, 28W 6D 4L, 86 GF — matches reality (90 pts, 28-6-4, 86-37)! Santos 74, Palmeiras 74 ✓ matches spec example. Grêmio... hmm real 2019: Grêmio had 65? Atlético-PR 64? Hmm — real 2019 table: 4. Grêmio 65? Actually let me not verify each — top-3 matches the spec's expected output exactly.\n\nLet me change threshold 0.8 → 0.85.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05c2566a8001qzALKqost