s... Let me just print the values.\n\n3. **test_find_cup_finals_by_stage** — let me see the error.\n\n4. Others: test_unknown_team (Real Madrid — wait! Real Madrid... is there a Real Madrid in the FIFA clubs? YES — FIFA has Real Madrid! So resolve(\"Real Madrid\") FINDS the FIFA entity → no QueryError → test fails. My test was wrong — use a truly unknown name like \"XYZ United FC\". Let me pick \"Gotham City FC\".\n\n5. test_find_player_by_name \"Gabriel Barbosa\" — FIFA 19 data: Gabriel Barbosa was at Inter Milan/Santos loan in FIFA 19... The FIFA 19 dataset: \"Gabriel Barbosa\"? The name in FIFA 19 is \"Gabriel Barbosa\" — but is he in the 18,207 players? His FIFA 19 rating ~79 at Inter. Hmm, but the search is substring — \"Gabriel Barbosa\" exact substring. Let me check the data.\n\n6. test_forwards_from_sao_paulo — position filter: \"FWD\" group check. Maybe São Paulo's forwards... FIFA São Paulo squad exists ✓ 20 players. Maybe my position matching has a bug: `if position_key: if player.position != position_key and player.position_group != group: continue` — for position=\"FWD\": position_key=\"FWD\"; player.position e.g. \"ST\" ≠ \"FWD\" and player.position_group \"FWD\" == group \"FWD\" → `!= group` False → condition False → don't skip ✓ keep. Looks right. Let me check what failed — maybe club resolution: \"São Paulo\" resolves ✓... or maybe zero forwards? São Paulo FIFA 19: forwards exist. Need to see the actual error.\n\n7. test_all_brazilian_teams_are_listable — expected >400 teams... let me check count of entities with match_count>0 and is_brazilian. We have 999 entities total; Brazilian with matches maybe ~500? Or the assertion `abc rn` in ids — ABC registered as \"abc rn\" ✓; \"remo pa\" ✓. Let me check the actual count.\n\nLet me debug all quickly.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05c3a0870001Iqk9MoRncu5Smt","sessionID":"ses_fa40f0460ffeYpKGnJPSwDwXVy","messageID":"msg_05c3980110014HuDp8E86Ot2TF"}}
