ch: Match) -> bool:\n+        labels = [\n+            label for label in (match.round_label, match.stage) if label\n+        ]\n+        keys = [label.casefold() for label in labels]\n+        return stage_key in keys or any(\n+            stage_key in key for key in keys\n+        )\n+\n+    exact = [\n         m for m in candidates\n-        if (m.round_label and stage_key in m.round_label.casefold())\n-        or (m.stage and stage_key in m.stage)\n+        if stage_key in [\n+            label.casefold()\n+            for label in (m.round_label, m.stage) if label\n+        ]\n     ]\n+    # exact stage matches win; fall back to substring (\"group\" ->\n+    # \"group stage\", \"semi\" -> \"semifinals\") only when nothing matched\n+    # exactly, so \"final\" never drags in quarterfinals.\n+    candidates = exact or [m for m in candidates if _stage_matches(m)]\n \n result: list[Match] = []\n seen_fixtures: set[tuple[str | None, str, str]] = set()\n for match in sorted(candidates, key=_match_sort_key):\n","additions":19,"deletions":3},"truncated":false},"title":"soccer_mcp/data_loader.py","time":{"start":1788253787538,"end":1788253787540}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Key findings:\n1. **São Paulo squad: 0 players!** — São Paulo FC is NOT in the FIFA 19 dataset clubs?! But earlier my club scan showed... let me re-check. Earlier I searched clubs containing 'paulo' and found only 'América FC (Minas Gerais)'... no \"São Paulo\"! Wait — earlier output of Brazilian clubs in FIFA: 'Atlético Mineiro', 'Atlético Paranaense', 'Bahia', 'Botafogo', 'Cruzeiro', 'Fluminense', 'Grêmio', 'Internacional', 'Santos', 'Santos Laguna'... NO São Paulo, NO Palmeiras, NO Corinthians, NO Flamengo, NO Vasco! Because FIFA 19 didn't license the Brazilian league fully — Brazilian clubs in FIFA 19 have GENERIC players. Hmm wait, but Santos IS there ('Santos' 20 players). So the licensed Brazilian clubs in this FIFA data: América-MG, Atlético-MG, Atlético-PR(Athletico?), Bahia, Botafogo, Ceará, Chapecoense, Cruzeiro, Fluminense, Grêmio, Internacional, Paraná, Santos, Sport, Vitória. NOT São Paulo / Corinthians / Palmeiras / Flamengo / Vasco.\n\nSo:\n- \"Show me all forwards from São Paulo FC\" → 0 results (with honest note). My BDD test asserting >0 must change: test that the result is EMPTY + club resolves + FIFA coverage note appears in the tool output. And use Santos or Grêmio for the positive case.\n- \"Which players play for Flamengo?\" → 0 + note (already tested that way ✓).\n- test_cross_file_club_matching uses Grêmio/Internacional/Sport ✓ good choices.\n\n2. **Gabriel Barbosa not in data** — change test to Gabriel Jesus (in data at Manchester City) and add a not-found case for Gabriel Barbosa.\n\n3. Sample questions: \"Show me all forwards from São Paulo FC\" — the tool returns \"Players matching (club: São Paulo...): - No players found...\" + note. My sample test asserts len > 30 and no \"Could not answer\" — passes ✓. But hmm — for the spec's sake, maybe pick \"Santos\" for that sample question to show a positive answer, since São Paulo genuinely isn't covered. I'll change the sample question to Santos and add a separate sample question for São Paulo asserting the honest note? The sample test just checks answerability — \"São Paulo FC forwards\" IS answered (with the note explaining). Keep both: one positive (Santos), one negative-with-note (São Paulo). Actually — my test_sample_questions asserts \"Could not answer\" not in answer — the São Paulo case returns \"Players matching (club: São Paulo (SP); position: FWD):\\n- No players found for this filter in the FIFA dataset.\\n\\nNote: the FIFA dataset...\" — no \"Could not answer\" ✓ passes. Keep it and add the Santos one too.\n\n4. **Fix BDD tests**:\n   - test_find_player_by_name: Gabriel Jesus positive + Gabriel Barbosa not-found.\n   - test_forwards_from_sao_paulo → rename to Santos forwards positive; add São Paulo negative.\n   - test_get