{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788253976565,"sessionID":"ses_fa40f0460ffeYpKGnJPSwDwXVy","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_002e69234be048bbab2ae787","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-e48763b54868/soccer_mcp/normalize.py","newString":"def parse_team_name(raw: str) -> ParsedTeamName:\n    \"\"\"Decompose a raw club spelling into ``base`` / ``state`` / ``country``.\n\n    Order of operations (important -- suffixes must be peeled off before the\n    base is cleaned):\n\n    1. trailing ``-XXX`` country tag (\"Barcelona-EQU\");\n    2. trailing 2-letter UF (\"Palmeiras-SP\", \"América - MG\", \"Botafogo PB\")\n       -- also runs after step 3 so \"X (antigo Y) - RJ\" works;\n    3. trailing parenthetical: a 2-letter UF (\"(PI)\"), a state name\n       (\"(Minas Gerais)\") or a country code (\"(URU)\") is promoted to\n       ``state``/``country``; anything else (e.g. \"(antigo Esporte Clube\n       Barreira)\") is dropped as a remark.\n    \"\"\"\n    text = raw.strip()\n    state: str | None = None\n    country: str | None = None\n\n    match = _RE_COUNTRY_SUFFIX.search(text)\n    if match and match.group(1).casefold() in COUNTRY_CODES:\n        country = match.group(1).casefold()\n        text = text[: match.start()].strip()\n\n    if state is None and country is None:\n        match = _RE_STATE_SUFFIX.search(text)\n        if match and match.group(1).casefold() in VALID_UFS:\n            state = match.group(1).casefold()\n            text = text[: match.start()].strip()\n\n    match = _RE_TRAILING_PAREN.search(text)\n    if match:\n        inner = strip_accents(match.group(1)).casefold().strip()\n        text = text[: match.start()].strip()\n        if inner in VALID_UFS and state is None:\n            state = inner\n        elif inner in STATE_NAMES and state is None:\n            state = STATE_NAMES[inner]\n        elif inner in COUNTRY_CODES and country is None:\n            country = inner\n        # any other parenthetical is a remark and is simply dropped\n\n    if state is None and country is None:\n        match = _RE_STATE_SUFFIX.search(text)\n        if match and match.group(1).casefold() in VALID_UFS:\n            state = match.group(1).casefold()\n            text = text[: match.start()].strip()\n\n    return ParsedTeamName(base=_clean_base(text), state=state, country=country)","oldString":"def parse_team_name(raw: str) -> ParsedTeamName:\n    \"\"\"Decompose a raw club spelling into ``base`` / ``state`` / ``country``.\n\n    Order of operations (important -- suffixes must be peeled off before the\n    base is cleaned):\n\n    1. trailing parenthetical: a 2-letter UF (\"(PI)\"), a state name\n       (\"(Minas Gerais)\") or a country code (\"(URU)\") is promoted to\n       ``state``/``country``; anything else (e.g. \"(antigo Esporte Clube\n       Barreira)\") is dropped;\n    2. trailing ``-XXX`` country tag (\"Barcelona-EQU\");\n    3. trailing 2-letter UF (\"Palmeiras-SP\", \"América - MG\", \"Botafogo PB\").\n    \"\"\"\n    text = raw.strip()\n    state: str | None = None\n    country: str | None = None\n\n    match = _RE_TRAILING_PAREN.search(text)\n    if match:\n        inner = strip_accents(match.group(1)).casefold().strip()\n        text = text[: match.start()].strip()\n        if inner in VALID_UFS:\n            state = inner\n        elif inner in STATE_NAMES:\n            state = STATE_NAMES[inner]\n        elif inner in COUNTRY_CODES:\n            country = inner\n\n    if country is None:\n        match = _RE_COUNTRY_SUFFIX.search(text)\n        if match and match.group(1).casefold() in COUNTRY_CODES:\n            country = match.group(1).casefold()\n            text = text[: match.start()].strip()\n\n    if state is None and country is None:\n        match = _RE_STATE_SUFFIX.search(text)\n        if match and match.group(1).casefold() in VALID_UFS:\n            state = match.group(1).casefold()\n            text = text[: match.start()].strip()\n\n    return ParsedTeamName(base=_clean_base(text), state=state, country=country)"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-e48763b54868/soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-e48763b54868/soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-e48763b54868/soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n@@ -163,36 +163,43 @@\n \n Order of operations (important -- suffixes must be peeled off before the\n base is cleaned):\n \n-1. trailing parenthetical: a 2-letter UF (\"(PI)\"), a state name\n+1. trailing ``-XXX`` country tag (\"Barcelona-EQU\");\n+2. trailing 2-letter UF (\"Palmeiras-SP\", \"América - MG\", \"Botafogo PB\")\n+   -- also runs after step 3 so \"X (antigo Y) - RJ\" works;\n+3. trailing parenthetical: a 2-letter UF (\"(PI)\"), a state name\n    (\"(Minas Gerais)\") or a country code (\"(URU)\") is promoted to\n    ``state``/``country``; anything else (e.g. \"(antigo Esporte Clube\n-   Barreira)\") is dropped;\n-2. trailing ``-XXX`` country tag (\"Barcelona-EQU\");\n-3. trailing 2-letter UF (\"Palmeiras-SP\", \"América - MG\", \"Botafogo PB\").\n+   Barreira)\") is dropped as a remark.\n \"\"\"\n text = raw.strip()\n state: str | None = None\n country: str | None = None\n \n+match = _RE_COUNTRY_SUFFIX.search(text)\n+if match and match.group(1).casefold() in COUNTRY_CODES:\n+    country = match.group(1).casefold()\n+    text = text[: match.start()].strip()\n+\n+if state is None and country is None:\n+    match = _RE_STATE_SUFFIX.search(text)\n+    if match and match.group(1).casefold() in VALID_UFS:\n+        state = match.group(1).casefold()\n+        text = text[: match.start()].strip()\n+\n match = _RE_TRAILING_PAREN.search(text)\n if match:\n     inner = strip_accents(match.group(1)).casefold().strip()\n     text = text[: match.start()].strip()\n-    if inner in VALID_UFS:\n+    if inner in VALID_UFS and state is None:\n         state = inner\n-    elif inner in STATE_NAMES:\n+    elif inner in STATE_NAMES and state is None:\n         state = STATE_NAMES[inner]\n-    elif inner in COUNTRY_CODES:\n+    elif inner in COUNTRY_CODES and country is None:\n         country = inner\n+    # any other parenthetical is a remark and is simply dropped\n \n-if country is None:\n-    match = _RE_COUNTRY_SUFFIX.search(text)\n-    if match and match.group(1).casefold() in COUNTRY_CODES:\n-        country = match.group(1).casefold()\n-        text = text[: match.start()].strip()\n-\n if state is None and country is None:\n     match = _RE_STATE_SUFFIX.search(text)\n     if match and match.group(1).casefold() in VALID_UFS:\n         state = match.group(1).casefold()\n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-e48763b54868/soccer_mcp/normalize.py","patch":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-e48763b54868/soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-e48763b54868/soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-e48763b54868/soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n@@ -163,36 +163,43 @@\n \n Order of operations (important -- suffixes must be peeled off before the\n base is cleaned):\n \n-1. trailing parenthetical: a 2-letter UF (\"(PI)\"), a state name\n+1. trailing ``-XXX`` country tag (\"Barcelona-EQU\");\n+2. trailing 2-letter UF (\"Palmeiras-SP\", \"América - MG\", \"Botafogo PB\")\n+   -- also runs after step 3 so \"X (antigo Y) - RJ\" works;\n+3. trailing parenthetical: a 2-letter UF (\"(PI)\"), a state name\n    (\"(Minas Gerais)\") or a country code (\"(URU)\") is promoted to\n    ``state``/``country``; anything else (e.g. \"(antigo Esporte Clube\n-   Barreira)\") is dropped;\n-2. trailing ``-XXX`` country tag (\"Barcelona-EQU\");\n-3. trailing 2-letter UF (\"Palmeiras-SP\", \"América - MG\", \"Botafogo PB\").\n+   Barreira)\") is dropped as a remark.\n \"\"\"\n text = raw.strip()\n state: str | None = None\n country: str | None = None\n \n+match = _RE_COUNTRY_SUFFIX.search(text)\n+if match and match.group(1).casefold() in COUNTRY_CODES:\n+    country = match.group(1).casefold()\n+    text = text[: match.start()].strip()\n+\n+if state is None and country is None:\n+    match = _RE_STATE_SUFFIX.search(text)\n+    if match and match.group(1).casefold() in VALID_UFS:\n+        state = match.group(1).casefold()\n+        text = text[: match.start()].strip()\n+\n match = _RE_TRAILING_PAREN.search(text)\n if match:\n     inner = strip_accents(match.group(1)).casefold().strip()\n     text = text[: match.start()].strip()\n-    if inner in VALID_UFS:\n+    if inner in VALID_UFS and state is None:\n         state = inner\n-    elif inner in STATE_NAMES:\n+    elif inner in STATE_NAMES and state is None:\n         state = STATE_NAMES[inner]\n-    elif inner in COUNTRY_CODES:\n+    elif inner in COUNTRY_CODES and country is None:\n         country = inner\n+    # any other parenthetical is a remark and is simply dropped\n \n-if country is None:\n-    match = _RE_COUNTRY_SUFFIX.search(text)\n-    if match and match.group(1).casefold() in COUNTRY_CODES:\n-        country = match.group(1).casefold()\n-        text = text[: match.start()].strip()\n-\n if state is None and country is None:\n     match = _RE_STATE_SUFFIX.search(text)\n     if match and match.group(1).casefold() in VALID_UFS:\n         state = match.group(1).casefold()\n","additions":20,"deletions":13},"truncated":false},"title":"soccer_mcp/normalize.py","time":{"start":1788253976560,"end":1788253976563}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Santos has 3 STs — so `search_players(club=\"Santos\", position=\"FWD\")` should return them. But it returned 0! Bug in my filter logic:\n\n```python\nif position_key:\n    if player.position != position_key and player.position_group != group:\n        continue\n```\n\nWith position_key=\"FWD\", group=position_group(\"FWD\")... **`position_group(\"FWD\")` returns None!** Because \"FWD\" is a GROUP name, not a FIFA position code — `_GROUP_BY_POSITION` has no \"FWD\" key → None. So for player.position=\"ST\": `player.position != \"FWD\"` → True; `player.position_group != None` → \"FWD\" != None → True → `True and True` → skip! BUG.\n\nFix: compute `group = position_group(position_key)` only when position_key is an actual code; better:\n```python\nif position_key:\n    wanted = {position_key} | set(POSITION_GROUPS.get(position_key, ()))\n    if player.position not in wanted:\n        continue\n```\nSo if user passes \"FWD\" → wanted = {\"FWD\",\"ST\",\"LS\",\"RS\",\"CF\",\"LW\",\"RW\",\"LF\",\"RF\"} ✓. If user passes \"ST\" → wanted = {\"ST\"} ✓. If \"GK\" → {\"GK\",\"GK\"} = {\"GK\"} ✓. \n\nFix in both `search_players` and `top_players` in queries.py.\n\nAnd fix parse_team_name paren handling. Let me rewrite that section:\n\n```python\ntext = raw.strip()\nstate = country = None\n\ndef _try_paren(text):\n    # returns (updated_text, state, country)\n    m = _RE_TRAILING_PAREN.search(text)\n    if not m: return text, None, None\n    inner = strip_accents(m.group(1)).casefold().strip()\n    if inner in VALID_UFS: return text[:m.start()].strip(), inner, None\n    if inner in STATE_NAMES: return text[:m.start()].strip(), STATE_NAMES[inner], None\n    if inner in COUNTRY_CODES: return text[:m.start()].strip(), None, inner\n    # non-geographic parenthetical -> drop it\n    return text[:m.start()].strip(), None, None\n\n# first pass: trailing paren (e.g. \"Nacional (URU)\", \"América FC (Minas Gerais)\")\n# but careful: \"(...)\" only counts when at END of raw (no suffix after it)\n```\n\nOrder matters for \"Boavista Sport Club (antigo...) - RJ\": state suffix first (peels \"- RJ\"), then trailing paren \"(antigo...)\" — droppable → \"boavista sport club\" ✓.\nFor \"América FC (Minas Gerais)\": no suffix → paren is state name → mg ✓.\nFor \"Nacional (URU)\": paren → country ✓.\nFor \"River (PI)\": paren → state pi ✓.\nFor hypothetical \"X (antigo Y) - RJ\": state then paren-drop ✓.\n\nBut what about paren NOT at end and NOT after suffix? e.g. \"Boavista Sport Club (antigo Esporte Clube Barreira) - RJ\" — after state peel, paren IS at end ✓. What if \"(antigo...)\" is mid-string with no suffix? e.g. \"Club (old) Something\"? Rare/none — leave (kept in base... would be ugly). Acceptable.\n\nNew flow:\n1. Try country suffix `-XXX`.\n2. Try state suffix `-XX`.\n3. Try trailing paren → promote or drop.\n4. If state still None and country None → try state suffix again (for \"X (PI) - YY\" weirdness? no — \"X (PI)\" would have promoted PI as state in step 3... then done).\n\nHmm wait — there's an interplay: \"Barcelona-EQU\" step 1 peels. \"Nacional (URU)\" step 1 no, step 2: state suffix regex on \"Nacional (URU)\" — trailing \"URU\" is 3 letters... `(?:^|\\s|[-\\u2013])\\s*([A-Za-z]{2})\\s*$` — needs separator + exactly 2 letters at end: \"(URU)\" ends with \")\" — regex needs `[A-Za-z]{2}$` — \")\" isn't a letter → no match ✓. Then step 3 paren → country ✓.\n\n\"River (PI)\" → step 2: trailing \")\" no match ✓ → step 3: paren \"PI\" → state ✓.\n\nBut careful — what about \"Guaraní (PAR)\"? step 3 → country par ✓.\n\nWhat about a paren mid-string like \"São Paulo (SP) FC\"? Doesn't exist. OK.\n\nAlso need loop: after step 3 drop, maybe another suffix appears? e.g. \"X (antigo Y) - RJ\" → step 2 peels \"- RJ\"?? wait — \"(antigo Y) - RJ\": step 2 regex looks for separator+2letters at END: \"- RJ\" ✓ peels → \"X (antigo Y)\" → step 3 drops paren → \"X\" ✓. \n\nWhat about \"X (Minas Gerais) - MG\"? → step 2 peels MG, step 3 promotes paren state (same) — fine.\n\nEdge: state names with spaces in parens \"(Rio de Janeiro)\" → STATE_NAMES has it ✓.\n\nImplement: replace the paren/suffix section with this sequence. Also keep _RE_COUNTRY_SUFFIX first (it's 3 letters; state regex can't match 3-letter endings).\n\nOne more: `_RE_STATE_SUFFIX` on \"A.b.c. - RN\": separator \"-\" + \"RN\" ✓ → base \"a.b.c.\" → \"abc\" ✓ (already worked).\n\nLet me rewrite parse_team_name.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05c3e37e0001BDztn8JZ8qBcGg","sessionID":"ses_fa40f0460ffeYpKGnJPSwDwXVy","messageID":"msg_05c3d5de6001hqxTBB9qLbrwS5"}}
