{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788254110824,"sessionID":"ses_fa40f0460ffeYpKGnJPSwDwXVy","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_2dd159eea5b144af96c8b56e","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-e48763b54868/soccer_mcp/data_loader.py","newString":"    def _display_name(self, raw_name: str, team_id: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Human-friendly display: keep accents, avoid duplicated state marks.\"\"\"\n        parsed = parse_team_name(raw_name)\n        display = raw_name.strip()\n        state = parsed.state\n        if state is None and \" \" in team_id and team_id.rsplit(\" \", 1)[1] in VALID_UFS:\n            state = team_id.rsplit(\" \", 1)[1]\n        if state:\n            # only append \"(XX)\" when the raw spelling doesn't already carry it\n            raw_folded = strip_accents(display).casefold()\n            if not raw_folded.endswith(state) and not raw_folded.endswith(f\"- {state}\"):\n                return f\"{display} ({state.upper()})\"\n        return display","oldString":"    def _display_name(self, raw_name: str, team_id: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Human-friendly display: strip a trailing state marker, keep accents.\"\"\"\n        parsed = parse_team_name(raw_name)\n        display = raw_name.strip()\n        # Re-attach the state in a clean \"(XX)\" form when the raw name had one\n        # or the id carries it.\n        state = parsed.state\n        if state is None and \" \" in team_id and team_id.rsplit(\" \", 1)[1] in {\n            \"ac\", \"al\", \"ap\", \"am\", \"ba\", \"ce\", \"df\", \"es\", \"go\", \"ma\", \"mt\",\n            \"ms\", \"mg\", \"pa\", \"pb\", \"pr\", \"pe\", \"pi\", \"rj\", \"rn\", \"rs\", \"ro\",\n            \"rr\", \"sc\", \"sp\", \"se\", \"to\",\n        }:\n            state = team_id.rsplit(\" \", 1)[1]\n        base = parsed.base\n        if state:\n            return f\"{display} ({state.upper()})\"\n        return display"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-e48763b54868/soccer_mcp/data_loader.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-e48763b54868/soccer_mcp/data_loader.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-e48763b54868/soccer_mcp/data_loader.py\n@@ -135,23 +135,19 @@\n \n # -- pass 2 ---------------------------------------------------------------\n \n def _display_name(self, raw_name: str, team_id: str) -> str:\n-    \"\"\"Human-friendly display: strip a trailing state marker, keep accents.\"\"\"\n+    \"\"\"Human-friendly display: keep accents, avoid duplicated state marks.\"\"\"\n     parsed = parse_team_name(raw_name)\n     display = raw_name.strip()\n-    # Re-attach the state in a clean \"(XX)\" form when the raw name had one\n-    # or the id carries it.\n     state = parsed.state\n-    if state is None and \" \" in team_id and team_id.rsplit(\" \", 1)[1] in {\n-        \"ac\", \"al\", \"ap\", \"am\", \"ba\", \"ce\", \"df\", \"es\", \"go\", \"ma\", \"mt\",\n-        \"ms\", \"mg\", \"pa\", \"pb\", \"pr\", \"pe\", \"pi\", \"rj\", \"rn\", \"rs\", \"ro\",\n-        \"rr\", \"sc\", \"sp\", \"se\", \"to\",\n-    }:\n+    if state is None and \" \" in team_id and team_id.rsplit(\" \", 1)[1] in VALID_UFS:\n         state = team_id.rsplit(\" \", 1)[1]\n-    base = parsed.base\n     if state:\n-        return f\"{display} ({state.upper()})\"\n+        # only append \"(XX)\" when the raw spelling doesn't already carry it\n+        raw_folded = strip_accents(display).casefold()\n+        if not raw_folded.endswith(state) and not raw_folded.endswith(f\"- {state}\"):\n+            return f\"{display} ({state.upper()})\"\n     return display\n \n def register(self, raw_name: str, source: str, *, weight: int = 1, is_club: bool = False) -> str:\n     \"\"\"Resolve ``raw_name`` to a team id, creating the entity if needed.\"\"\"\n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-e48763b54868/soccer_mcp/data_loader.py","patch":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-e48763b54868/soccer_mcp/data_loader.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-e48763b54868/soccer_mcp/data_loader.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-e48763b54868/soccer_mcp/data_loader.py\n@@ -135,23 +135,19 @@\n \n # -- pass 2 ---------------------------------------------------------------\n \n def _display_name(self, raw_name: str, team_id: str) -> str:\n-    \"\"\"Human-friendly display: strip a trailing state marker, keep accents.\"\"\"\n+    \"\"\"Human-friendly display: keep accents, avoid duplicated state marks.\"\"\"\n     parsed = parse_team_name(raw_name)\n     display = raw_name.strip()\n-    # Re-attach the state in a clean \"(XX)\" form when the raw name had one\n-    # or the id carries it.\n     state = parsed.state\n-    if state is None and \" \" in team_id and team_id.rsplit(\" \", 1)[1] in {\n-        \"ac\", \"al\", \"ap\", \"am\", \"ba\", \"ce\", \"df\", \"es\", \"go\", \"ma\", \"mt\",\n-        \"ms\", \"mg\", \"pa\", \"pb\", \"pr\", \"pe\", \"pi\", \"rj\", \"rn\", \"rs\", \"ro\",\n-        \"rr\", \"sc\", \"sp\", \"se\", \"to\",\n-    }:\n+    if state is None and \" \" in team_id and team_id.rsplit(\" \", 1)[1] in VALID_UFS:\n         state = team_id.rsplit(\" \", 1)[1]\n-    base = parsed.base\n     if state:\n-        return f\"{display} ({state.upper()})\"\n+        # only append \"(XX)\" when the raw spelling doesn't already carry it\n+        raw_folded = strip_accents(display).casefold()\n+        if not raw_folded.endswith(state) and not raw_folded.endswith(f\"- {state}\"):\n+            return f\"{display} ({state.upper()})\"\n     return display\n \n def register(self, raw_name: str, source: str, *, weight: int = 1, is_club: bool = False) -> str:\n     \"\"\"Resolve ``raw_name`` to a team id, creating the entity if needed.\"\"\"\n","additions":6,"deletions":10},"truncated":false},"title":"soccer_mcp/data_loader.py","time":{"start":1788254110819,"end":1788254110821}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Outputs look great and match the spec's example formats. One display nit: \"Flamengo-RJ (RJ)\" is redundant — the raw variant \"Flamengo-RJ\" already contains the state, and my display logic appends \" (RJ)\". Fix `TeamRegistry._display_name`: if the raw name already ends with the state marker (\"-RJ\", \" - RJ\"), don't append \"(RJ)\" — just use the raw as-is. Actually — the spec examples use plain \"Flamengo\". Hmm: display \"Flamengo-RJ\" (raw) vs \"Flamengo (RJ)\"? The spec's example: \"Flamengo 2-1 Fluminense\". For cleaner output matching the spec, I could use the base display (accent-restored?) — but accent restoration is hard generically. Compromise: if raw ends with the state suffix, keep raw as-is (\"Flamengo-RJ\", \"América - MG\"); if raw is bare and state known → append \" (RJ)\" (\"Flamengo (RJ)\" hmm...). Wait — the entity display is a single name chosen once from the most common variant. The most common variant for flamengo rj is \"Flamengo-RJ\" (brasileirao) or \"Flamengo\"... counts: brasileirao has \"Flamengo-RJ\" hundreds; Libertadores \"Flamengo\" ~90; novo \"Flamengo\"; br_football \"Flamengo\"; FIFA none. So most common = \"Flamengo-RJ\".\n\nHonestly \"Flamengo-RJ\" reads fine and is unambiguous. The double \"Flamengo-RJ (RJ)\" is the problem. Fix: in _display_name, only append \" (XX)\" when the raw variant does NOT already end with that state marker. Let me implement: check raw (after strip) case-insensitively ends with the state code preceded by separator or space.\n\nAlso \"Corinthians-SP (SP)\" same issue → \"Corinthians-SP\" ✓. \"Nacional (URU)\" ends with \"(URU)\" — country; current logic appends state only; country None → no append ✓ stays \"Nacional (URU)\" ✓.\n\nLet me fix _display_name.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05c404453001MRg1XZYPuNfHd6","sessionID":"ses_fa40f0460ffeYpKGnJPSwDwXVy","messageID":"msg_05c3fd352001b7PUGNNMKdX4D4"}}
