{"type":"text","timestamp":1788254424430,"sessionID":"ses_fa40f0460ffeYpKGnJPSwDwXVy","part":{"id":"prt_05c44e1570014z5wEKdJAOUDDF","messageID":"msg_05c44cc04001eA9Pc3x5yIUUq5","sessionID":"ses_fa40f0460ffeYpKGnJPSwDwXVy","type":"text","text":"Done. The Brazilian Soccer MCP Server from TASK.md is fully implemented and verified.\n\n**What was built**\n\n- **`server.py`** — MCP server (official `mcp` SDK v2, stdio transport) exposing **20 tools** covering all five required capability categories: match queries, team queries, player queries, competition queries, and statistical analysis.\n- **`soccer_mcp/`** — `normalize.py` (folds every team-name convention onto canonical ids: state suffixes, dot abbreviations like `C. R. B. - AL`, parentheticals, full legal names, foreign country tags, historical renames, nicknames; multi-format date parsing), `data_loader.py` (loads all 6 CSVs in ~1s, two-pass team registry, cross-file dedup with a completeness-guarded source priority), `queries.py`, `formatting.py` (spec's example answer formats), `tools.py`, `bdd.py`.\n- **`tests/`** — 113 BDD Given/When/Then pytest scenarios, including the spec's exact Gherkin scenarios, in-memory MCP-protocol tests, a real stdio subprocess boot test, 32 answerable sample questions (spec requires ≥20), and performance checks (all pass with wide margins).\n\n**Verification highlights**\n\n- 2019 Brasileirão standings computed from matches reproduce reality exactly: Flamengo 90 pts (28W-6D-4L) champion, Santos/Palmeiras 74 — matching the spec's example output.\n- Dedup works: Série A 2019 (present in 3 files) returns exactly 380 matches; Copa do Brasil 2021 auto-falls back to the complete BR-Football file since the cup file's late rounds are `NA`.\n- Cross-source data bugs handled: COVID-season spillover (Jan–Mar → prior season), the cancelled 2016 Chapecoense match, penalties-decided finals reported honestly, River Plate kept separate from River Plate-SE.\n- Final state: `113 passed`, pyflakes-clean, and a live stdio boot answering champion/player/derby questions correctly.\n\nThe updated README documents architecture, all tools, run instructions, and honest data-quality limitations (e.g. FIFA-19-era player data lacks Flamengo/Corinthians/Palmeiras squads).","time":{"start":1788254413143,"end":1788254424427}}}
